  "body": "Both http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.cpp#836 and Chrome source code indicate that the \";(\" sequence means something special in MIME types and it looks like parsing is supposed to stop there, due to some legacy MIME type comment feature.\r\n\r\nHowever, when I try something like\r\n```\r\nHTTP/1.1 200\r\nContent-Length: 55\r\nContent-Type: text/html;test=test;(;charset=gbk\r\n\r\n<script>document.write(document.characterSet)</script>\r\n```\r\nbrowsers consistently end up not ignoring the `charset` parameter, so I'm not sure what is going on.\r\n\r\n@mcmanus @sleevi help appreciated.",
